guest receipt, order privacy, and customer history (future consideration, not implemented)
- Guests and logged-in customers receive a receipt after confirmed payment.
- Guest checkout records the created order ID in the browser's server-side Laravel session, including orders still awaiting payment.
- Every guest order status, receipt, and download request checks that the session is allowed to access that order. Knowing or sharing the order URL/ID alone does not grant access.
- Guest access lasts while that browser session remains valid; clearing cookies, session expiry, or another browser/device loses access. Staff can help retrieve the order through authenticated staff tools.
- Customer login is separate from staff login. Logged-in customers can see their own order history and receipts across devices, with account ownership checked on the backend.
- Keep existing staff login and role permissions for staff access. Payment confirmation still comes from verified backend payment processing.
